  "coverage": [
    "Exact upstream Poseidon2 duplex observation, base/extension and bit sampling, pending-state snapshots, and deterministic minimum-witness grinding.",
    "Resident observation ranges canonicalize on CUDA, reject invalid ownership and state/input aliasing, and resident samples feed CUDA commitments without host transfer.",
    "Whole-operation byte/allocation-count admission, bounded snapshots, runtime failure, abandoned proof attempts, exhaustion, injected partial failures and unwind retire the shared family.",
    "CUDA CandidateChallenger implements the existing observation, sampling, cloning, grinding and attempt interfaces with no CPU fallback on failure.",
    "A small multiplication AIR uses the production hiding PCS and security profile with a CUDA challenger; its Postcard proof round-trips into the unchanged CPU proof type, verifies independently, and rejects altered public inputs.",
    "Independent verification does not issue CUDA commands; default wallet/recursive configurations are unchanged.",
    "Shared OpenCL transcript constants preserve their values; six host and three OpenCL challenger device tests pass.",
    "All existing native primitives, shared matrix planner tests, OpenCL quotient/specialization regressions, CPU/OpenCL checks, Apple Metal cross-compilation and standalone CUDA builds pass.",
    "NVRTC compiles the new native transcript kernels for compute_70 and compute_120; only sm_120 executes locally."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The proof integration test uses CUDA only for the transcript/challenger. It is not full CUDA proving and establishes no transaction throughput.",
    "Native scalar derivations, randomness/hiding, witness/preprocessing/lookup, openings/FRI/final-polynomial work, complete PCS/backend and stage reporting, persistent worker admission and pool integration remain unfinished.",
    "No V100 execution qualification or Apple Metal execution is available on this host.",
    "Public challenge samples may be read back through the generic challenger adapter; device samples remain available for future native pipeline integration.",
    "Initial compilation failed on a nonexistent bincode dependency; the test was corrected to the existing Postcard format without adding a dependency. Failed build evidence is retained."
  ],
